The variance is the cluster-robust CR1 estimator, \code{G / (G - 1) (n - 1) / (n - K)} times the sandwich, \code{K} counting the regressors, the constant,
and the levels less one of each fixed effect not nested in a cluster;
with two kinds of cluster it is \code{V1 + V2 - V12} (Cameron, Gelbach and
Miller 2011) with \code{G} the smaller number of clusters. Tests and intervals
